            <ArticleTitle>Ventricular tachycardia following tube thoracotomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1504-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/europace/euq172</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Arrhythmias provoked by tube thoracotomy are a rare complication. We report a ventricular tachycardia after chest tube insertion for a device-related pneumothorax. Sinus rhythm was restored only by removal of the chest tube and insertion of a pliable pleural drain. Identification of the chest tube as an arrhythmic trigger following tube thoracotomy is essential in definitive management of refractory arrhythmias.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
